<article class="env-proposition" id="06BT">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06BT">Proposition <span data-tag="06BT">7.6.6.39</span> <span class="named">(Transitivity)</span>.</a> Let $\mathbb {K}$ be a collection of simplicial sets and let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and $V: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete inner fibrations of simplicial sets. If $V$ is a cocartesian fibration, then the composition $(U \circ V): \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is also $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      By virtue of Remark <a data-tag="06BS" href="/tag/06BS">7.6.6.38</a>, we may assume without loss of generality that $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is an $\infty $-category (or even that $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}= \Delta ^1$), so that $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ are also $\infty $-categories. Fix an object $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, a simplicial set $K \in \mathbb {K}$, and a diagram $q: K \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{C}$; we will show that $q$ admits an extension $\overline{q}: K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{C}$ which is a $(U \circ V)$-colimit diagram in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$. Set $q_0 = V \circ q$. Our assumption that $U$ is $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete guarantees that $q_0$ admits an extension $\overline{q}_0: K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{C}$ which is a $U$-colimit diagram. Using Example <a data-tag="06BR" href="/tag/06BR">7.6.6.37</a>, we see that the lifting problem 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ K \ar [d] \ar [r]^-{q} &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\ar [d]^{V} \\ K^{\triangleright } \ar@ {--&gt;}[ur]^{ \overline{q} } \ar [r]^-{ \overline{q}_0} &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \]
</div>
<p>
       admits a solution, where $\overline{q}$ is a $V$-colimit diagram in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$. Applying Proposition <a data-tag="02KQ" href="/tag/02KQ">7.1.6.10</a>, we conclude that $\overline{q}$ is also a $(V \circ U)$-colimit diagram. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
